From e40b37304eeafb478198b36377eeecd52369df29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corvid <corvid@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:48:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Corvid v1.8: line quality of the streams sent to this server

New package linehealth: for every RTMP and SRT publisher (keys
"rtmp:<name>", "srt:<resource>") the last 10 minutes of gaps (>= 1 s
without data) and dropped connections (a publisher that came back within
a minute; one that stays away was stopped on purpose). Levels: good,
unstable, bad (2 drops, 10 s without data in total, a 5 s gap or a 5 s
stall right now). The history survives configuration reloads.

GET /api/v3/fork/linehealth.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UhjysExATCKDyVfUWLA89B
